{:edb/committed true :edb/basis-t 2867 :edb/replayed false :edb/tx-hash "f16e4bde45c73174f5bdc4011bee1483a98975282d90b1ba35421d073c19699c" :edb/db-before-t 2866 :edb/db-after-t 2867 :edb/tx-data [[13194139536179 50 #inst "2026-10-09T18:26:53.466Z" 13194139536179 true] [17592186152071 1020 #edb/ref 17592186387516 13194139536179 true] [17592186152071 1020 #edb/ref 17592186387523 13194139536179 true] [17592186152071 1020 #edb/ref 17592186387530 13194139536179 true] [17592186152072 1020 #edb/ref 17592186387509 13194139536179 true] [17592186152072 1020 #edb/ref 17592186387537 13194139536179 true] [17592186387509 1017 #edb/ref 17592186387510 13194139536179 true] [17592186387509 1089 "q-122964" 13194139536179 true] [17592186387509 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139536179 true] [17592186387509 1100 "Let $R=[0,2]\\times [0,2]$ be a region in the $xy$-plane, and let $f(x,y)=9-{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}.$\nFurther, let $P$ be a partition of $R,$ where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{1}={0,1,2},\\,{P}_{2}={0,1,2},\\,P={P}_{1}\\times {P}_{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCalculate the lower Riemann sum $L(f,P).$" 13194139536179 true] [17592186387509 1113 #uuid "c70dbc22-a4b5-5480-a11f-1031f28c8756" 13194139536179 true] [17592186387509 1145 "First, let's draw the region $R$ and the partition $P.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14083084/assets/3cac974f7352243bfbe008ad8af58ae8222709f81f434070383cc759a46747c7.png)\n\nThe lower Riemann sum $L(f,P)$ is given by\n\n$$\nL(f,P)={m}_{11}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{11})+{m}_{21}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{21})+{m}_{12}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{12})+{m}_{22}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{22})\n$$\n\nwhere ${m}_{ij}$ is the minimum value of $f$ in each subregion ${R}_{ij}.$ We pick the *minimum* value of $f$ because we're finding the *lower* sum.\n\nTaking into account the fact that $\\text{Area}({R}_{ij})=1$ for all $4$ subregions, the formula for $L(f,P)$ reduces to\n\n$$\nL(f,P)={m}_{11}+{m}_{21}+{m}_{12}+{m}_{22}.\n$$\n\nNow, notice that\n\n- $f(x,y)=9-{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}$ decreases as $x$ increases, and\n\n- $f(x,y)=9-{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}$ decreases as $y$ increases.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14083084/assets/0fefe892c74e8d391e56ee822f83e7e0fe0110593c9d6a4b93b8cfe1e558ab16.png)\n\nAs a result, the *minimum* value of $f$ in each subregion is attained when we have the *largest* possible $x$ and the *largest* possible $y.$ This is the value at the *top right corner* of each subregion.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14083084/assets/fe872f1f1b0307760dcdba6ac6f6be20f197662ac250ab46dc77fa472295906f.png)\n\nHence:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{m}_{11} & =f(1,1)=7 \\\\ {m}_{21} & =f(2,1)=4 \\\\ {m}_{12} & =f(1,2)=4 \\\\ {m}_{22} & =f(2,2)=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\nL(f,P)=7+4+4+1=16.\n$$" 13194139536179 true] [17592186387510 1000 #edb/ref 17592186387511 13194139536179 true] [17592186387510 1000 #edb/ref 17592186387512 13194139536179 true] [17592186387510 1000 #edb/ref 17592186387513 13194139536179 true] [17592186387510 1000 #edb/ref 17592186387514 13194139536179 true] [17592186387510 1000 #edb/ref 17592186387515 13194139536179 true] [17592186387510 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139536179 true] [17592186387510 1041 "selection" 13194139536179 true] [17592186387510 1104 #edb/ref 17592186387512 13194139536179 true] [17592186387510 1110 #uuid "f07897ba-d1f0-5e68-8ef8-cd7504c064ad" 13194139536179 true] [17592186387511 1034 "12" 13194139536179 true] [17592186387511 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536179 true] [17592186387511 1111 #uuid "10f1a6b8-bc2c-5a80-8357-295783024abb" 13194139536179 true] [17592186387512 1034 "16" 13194139536179 true] [17592186387512 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536179 true] [17592186387512 1111 #uuid "a57e6895-e059-55cc-80d4-076bda8bbcbe" 13194139536179 true] [17592186387513 1034 "8" 13194139536179 true] [17592186387513 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536179 true] [17592186387513 1111 #uuid "a4864502-3f35-5e7f-a3e1-d0df7a16fa68" 13194139536179 true] [17592186387514 1034 "32" 13194139536179 true] [17592186387514 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536179 true] [17592186387514 1111 #uuid "573d87f6-891c-57dd-9c28-e62de3e6efc6" 13194139536179 true] [17592186387515 1034 "24" 13194139536179 true] [17592186387515 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536179 true] [17592186387515 1111 #uuid "a7a1377f-df64-552e-baf8-948fbafe555e" 13194139536179 true] [17592186387516 1017 #edb/ref 17592186387517 13194139536179 true] [17592186387516 1089 "q-122982" 13194139536179 true] [17592186387516 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139536179 true] [17592186387516 1100 "Let $R=[1,4]\\times [0,2]$ be a region in the $xy$-plane, and let $f(x,y)=x+{y}^{2}+2.$\nFurther, let $P$ be a partition of $R,$ where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{1}={1,2,3,4},\\,{P}_{2}={0,2},\\,P={P}_{1}\\times {P}_{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCalculate the lower Riemann sum $L(f,P).$" 13194139536179 true] [17592186387516 1113 #uuid "2917fbcf-2187-5853-8927-eace7c8bfe2c" 13194139536179 true] [17592186387516 1145 "First, let's draw the region $R$ and the partition $P.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14083084/assets/c30acb7cb94886e612675d5e64838961134e8d09e5d88c1d803067832f4b173e.png)\n\nThe lower sum $L(f,P)$ is given by\n\n$$\nL(f,P)={m}_{11}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{11})+{m}_{21}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{21})+{m}_{31}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{31})\n$$\n\nwhere ${m}_{ij}$ is the *minimum* value of $f$ in each subregion ${R}_{ij}.$ We pick the *minimum* value of $f$ because we're finding the *lower* sum.\n\nTaking into account the fact that $\\text{Area}({R}_{ij})=2$ for all $3$ subregions, the formula for $L(f,P)$ reduces to\n\n$$\nL(f,P)=2{m}_{11}+2{m}_{21}+2{m}_{31}.\n$$\n\nNow, notice that\n\n- $f(x,y)=x+{y}^{2}+2$ increases as $x$ increases, and\n\n- $f(x,y)=x+{y}^{2}+2$ increases as $y$ increases.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14083084/assets/e5c92768512480b16fcca735126b303c4ca372d22a5c735fc8cea1588a3c5811.png)\n\nAs a result, the *minimum* value of $f$ in each subregion is attained when we have the *smallest* possible $x$ and the *smallest* possible $y.$ This is the value at the *bottom left corner* of each subregion.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14083084/assets/b015f94b135ca669c0711057c7245982eb8f0257e4947a603571f2826364b8fa.png)\n\nHence:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{m}_{11} & =f(1,0)=3 \\\\ {m}_{21} & =f(2,0)=4 \\\\ {m}_{31} & =f(3,0)=5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(f,P) & =2\\cdot 3+2\\cdot 4+2\\cdot 5 \\\\  & =24.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139536179 true] [17592186387517 1000 #edb/ref 17592186387518 13194139536179 true] [17592186387517 1000 #edb/ref 17592186387519 13194139536179 true] [17592186387517 1000 #edb/ref 17592186387520 13194139536179 true] [17592186387517 1000 #edb/ref 17592186387521 13194139536179 true] [17592186387517 1000 #edb/ref 17592186387522 13194139536179 true] [17592186387517 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139536179 true] [17592186387517 1041 "selection" 13194139536179 true] [17592186387517 1104 #edb/ref 17592186387522 13194139536179 true] [17592186387517 1110 #uuid "7f76a934-c144-5429-b6ca-5c77d902fb9b" 13194139536179 true] [17592186387518 1034 "12" 13194139536179 true] [17592186387518 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536179 true] [17592186387518 1111 #uuid "97ad56ee-c6ac-577b-95cd-f34e1771756d" 13194139536179 true] [17592186387519 1034 "15" 13194139536179 true] [17592186387519 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536179 true] [17592186387519 1111 #uuid "9b155ead-8af5-52bb-b827-a826c304754b" 13194139536179 true] [17592186387520 1034 "30" 13194139536179 true] [17592186387520 1103 #edb/ref 175921860