 17592186045453 13194139536179 true] [17592186387527 1111 #uuid "c1d8dcbf-db25-58f9-83fb-5b70fca925d6" 13194139536179 true] [17592186387528 1034 "15" 13194139536179 true] [17592186387528 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536179 true] [17592186387528 1111 #uuid "927811f7-d6e8-55cb-b530-b216a6039fc8" 13194139536179 true] [17592186387529 1034 "21" 13194139536179 true] [17592186387529 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536179 true] [17592186387529 1111 #uuid "c836c950-1848-54ba-b6c0-ab0d5418b753" 13194139536179 true] [17592186387530 1017 #edb/ref 17592186387531 13194139536179 true] [17592186387530 1089 "q-75249" 13194139536179 true] [17592186387530 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139536179 true] [17592186387530 1100 "Let $R=[1,3]\\times [2,4]$ be a region in the $xy$-plane, and let $f(x,y)=2x+y.$\nFurther, let $P$ be a partition of $R,$ where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{1}={1,2,3},\\,{P}_{2}={2,3,4},\\,P={P}_{1}\\times {P}_{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCalculate the lower Riemann sum $L(f,P).$" 13194139536179 true] [17592186387530 1113 #uuid "d52aff52-1e67-52b2-affa-9c2158c1c6ee" 13194139536179 true] [17592186387530 1145 "First, let's draw the region $R$ and the partition $P.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14083084/assets/01edff0feb1bf7545526c3eb258ffb608a982fae094d83a0512b006ec930a60f.png)\n\nThe lower sum $L(f,P)$ is given by \n\n$$\nL(f,P)={m}_{11}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{11})+{m}_{21}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{21})+{m}_{12}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{12})+{m}_{22}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{22})\n$$\n\nwhere ${m}_{ij}$ is the *minimum* value of $f$ in each subregion ${R}_{ij}.$ We pick the *minimum* value of $f$ because we're finding the *lower* sum.\n\nTaking into account the fact that $\\text{Area}({R}_{ij})=1$ for all $4$ subregions, the formula for $L(f,P)$ reduces to\n\n$$\nL(f,P)={m}_{11}+{m}_{21}+{m}_{12}+{m}_{22}.\n$$\n\nNow, notice that\n\n- $f(x,y)=2x+y$ increases as $x$ increases, and\n\n- $f(x,y)=2x+y$ increases as $y$ increases.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14083084/assets/335148bb25604ed918640c6a21feb7de3ede3a2cd340fbc5288442bbe3ed3d6d.png)\n\nAs a result, the *minimum* value of $f$ in each subregion is attained when we have the *smallest* possible $x$ and the *smallest* possible $y.$ This is the value at the *bottom left corner* of each subregion.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14083084/assets/b0c98c2e3785d1b0ccdd8675f89f6a83372dfc1f1ca60c76c638871d56add91b.png)\n\nHence:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{m}_{11} & =f(1,2)=4 \\\\ {m}_{21} & =f(2,2)=6 \\\\ {m}_{12} & =f(1,3)=5 \\\\ {m}_{22} & =f(2,3)=7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(f,P) & =4+6+5+7 \\\\  & =22.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139536179 true] [17592186387531 1000 #edb/ref 17592186387532 13194139536179 true] [17592186387531 1000 #edb/ref 17592186387533 13194139536179 true] [17592186387531 1000 #edb/ref 17592186387534 13194139536179 true] [17592186387531 1000 #edb/ref 17592186387535 13194139536179 true] [17592186387531 1000 #edb/ref 17592186387536 13194139536179 true] [17592186387531 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139536179 true] [17592186387531 1041 "selection" 13194139536179 true] [17592186387531 1104 #edb/ref 17592186387532 13194139536179 true] [17592186387531 1110 #uuid "10013bee-bffd-5561-99b3-880256fe1e1e" 13194139536179 true] [17592186387532 1034 "22" 13194139536179 true] [17592186387532 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536179 true] [17592186387532 1111 #uuid "05d9a8d6-b403-569f-9a95-8044750dcfce" 13194139536179 true] [17592186387533 1034 "34" 13194139536179 true] [17592186387533 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536179 true] [17592186387533 1111 #uuid "31e60bfd-a28e-52e4-902c-a697474adc9d" 13194139536179 true] [17592186387534 1034 "11" 13194139536179 true] [17592186387534 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536179 true] [17592186387534 1111 #uuid "ce92c15b-ad1c-5b12-92dc-3eeb3d9c1eeb" 13194139536179 true] [17592186387535 1034 "30" 13194139536179 true] [17592186387535 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536179 true] [17592186387535 1111 #uuid "a0b7d59c-7836-5633-bc22-452bd79702fc" 13194139536179 true] [17592186387536 1034 "17" 13194139536179 true] [17592186387536 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536179 true] [17592186387536 1111 #uuid "1b87263a-2a28-5299-92ad-a550a47ab105" 13194139536179 true] [17592186387537 1017 #edb/ref 17592186387538 13194139536179 true] [17592186387537 1089 "q-75254" 13194139536179 true] [17592186387537 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139536179 true] [17592186387537 1100 "Let $R=[0,2]\\times [0,2]$ be a region in the $xy$-plane, and let $f(x,y)=8-{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}.$\nFurther, let $P$ be a partition of $R,$ where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{1}={0,1,2},\\,{P}_{2}={0,1,2},\\,P={P}_{1}\\times {P}_{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCalculate the lower Riemann sum $L(f,P).$" 13194139536179 true] [17592186387537 1113 #uuid "d7401229-63d2-5b7e-9354-110723dd0a06" 13194139536179 true] [17592186387537 1145 "First, let's draw the region $R$ and the partition $P.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14083084/assets/3cac974f7352243bfbe008ad8af58ae8222709f81f434070383cc759a46747c7.png)\n\nThe lower Riemann sum $L(f,P)$ is given by\n\n$$\nL(f,P)={m}_{11}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{11})+{m}_{21}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{21})+{m}_{12}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{12})+{m}_{22}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{22})\n$$\n\nwhere ${m}_{ij}$ is the minimum value of $f$ in each subregion ${R}_{ij}.$ We pick the *minimum* value of $f$ because we're finding the *lower* sum.\n\nTaking into account the fact that $\\text{Area}({R}_{ij})=1$ for all $4$ subregions, the formula for $L(f,P)$ reduces to\n\n$$\nL(f,P)={m}_{11}+{m}_{21}+{m}_{12}+{m}_{22}.\n$$\n\nNow, notice that\n\n- $f(x,y)=8-{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}$ decreases as $x$ increases, and\n\n- $f(x,y)=8-{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}$ decreases as $y$ increases.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14083084/assets/0fefe892c74e8d391e56ee822f83e7e0fe0110593c9d6a4b93b8cfe1e558ab16.png)\n\nAs a result, the *minimum* value of $f$ in each subregion is attained when we have the *largest* possible $x$ and the *largest* possible $y.$ This is the value at the *top right corner* of each subregion.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14083084/assets/fe872f1f1b0307760dcdba6ac6f6be20f197662ac250ab46dc77fa472295906f.png)\n\nHence:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{m}_{11} & =f(1,1)=6 \\\\ {m}_{21} & =f(2,1)=3 \\\\ {m}_{12} & =f(1,2)=3 \\\\ {m}_{22} & =f(2,2)=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\nL(f,P)=6+3+3+0=12.\n$$" 13194139536179 true] [17592186387538 1000 #edb/ref 17592186387539 13194139536179 true] [17592186387538 1000 #edb/ref 17592186387540 13194139536179 true] [17592186387538 1000 #edb/ref 17592186387541 13194139536179 true] [17592186387538 1000 #edb/ref 17592186387542 13194139536179 true] [17592186387538 1000 #edb/ref 17592186387543 13194139536179 true] [17592186387538 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139536179 true] [17592186387538 1041 "selection" 13194139536179 true] [17592186387538 1104 #edb/ref 17592186387539 13194139536179 true] [17592186387538 1110 #uuid "38ab7d44-8beb-5061-ad5c-dce6e5437b37" 13194139536179 true] [17592186387539 1034 "12" 13194139536179 true] [17592186387539 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536179 true] [17592186387539 1111 #uuid "4e485936-79cd-51b3-8faa-dbb36a81f646" 13194139536179 true] [17592186387540 1034 "10" 13194139536179 true] [17592186387540 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536179 true] [17592186387540 1111 #uuid "032f704d-bbd8-51f2-9675-cf7e8147a4f3" 13194139536179 true] [17592186387541 1034 "16" 13194139536179 true] [17592186387541 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536179 true] [17592186387541 1111 